  "blocks": [
    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-1.6.03-01",
      "block_type": "definition",
      "heading": "Weather instruments",
      "text": "A weather station uses different instruments because temperature, rainfall, humidity, pressure, wind and sunshine are different variables. Identify the instrument from its working parts and purpose, not simply its position in a familiar picture. A funnel and collecting vessel suggest a rain gauge, paired thermometers with a wet covering suggest a psychrometer, and rotating cups suggest an anemometer. The unit belongs with the variable: degrees Celsius for temperature, millimetres for rainfall depth, hectopascals for pressure and an appropriate speed unit for wind. An instrument name without its measured element is incomplete understanding.",
