    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-1.6.03-02",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "A rain gauge collects precipitation through an opening of known area. In a simple manual design, a funnel directs water into a container that is emptied into a suitable graduated measuring cylinder. The cylinder or system is calibrated to express rainfall as an equivalent depth over the collecting area. Rainfall depth is not the same as the raw depth of water in any arbitrary bottle. A narrow cylinder can contain a deeper column than the amount of rain represented, because the funnel has collected water from a wider area. Use the supplied calibration rather than treating the apparatus as an unscaled container.",
