    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-1.6.03-03",
      "block_type": "worked_application",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "The gauge rim should be level and appropriately exposed, with nearby obstacles and splash effects considered. Trees can intercept water or drip into the opening; buildings can shelter it or disturb airflow. A blocked funnel, tilted gauge or unrecorded overflow can reduce the reliability of the result. In a manual method, read at the defined time, record the interval and empty or reset according to the procedure. A gauge containing two days of rain cannot be labelled a one-day total unless the collection history supports that interval. Missing or compromised readings should be marked rather than converted into zero rainfall.",
