    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-1.6.03-05",
      "block_type": "worked_application",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "An original instrument resource might label the maximum index at 28°C, the minimum at 12°C and the current reading at 20°C. Maximum and minimum refer to the interval since reset, not to future forecasts. The daily range for a correctly specified daily interval is 28 − 12 = 16°C. Reading the current 20°C as the maximum would confuse the variable being recorded. A question image should leave indices and scales readable; a low-resolution drawing that makes 26 and 28 indistinguishable cannot support a precise numerical answer fairly.",
