    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-1.6.03-07",
      "block_type": "worked_application",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Relative humidity is obtained using the dry-bulb temperature, wet-bulb depression and an appropriate supplied table or calculation. Do not interpret the depression itself as a percentage. For example, dry bulb 25°C and wet bulb 20°C give a depression of 5°C. If the supplied table for the stated conditions gives 63%, that is the relative humidity value to report. A different table or pressure assumption can affect the conversion, so use the resource provided. The wet-bulb temperature is not automatically the dew point, although they coincide with air temperature at saturation in the relevant limit.",
