    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-1.6.03-14",
      "block_type": "worked_application",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "An original card can show burn intervals from 08:00–10:00, 11:00–13:30 and 15:00–16:30. Their durations are 2, 2.5 and 1.5 hours, giving six hours in total. Adding the whole interval from 08:00 to 16:30 would incorrectly include the unburnt gaps. A drawing should show the time scale clearly enough to support that reading. Likewise, a sunshine graph labelled hours cannot be interpreted as rainfall in millimetres just because both quantities use bars in some other diagram. Axis labels and units determine the variable.",
