      "block_type": "worked_application",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "An original matching resource can include a funnel-and-vessel instrument, paired wet/dry thermometers, a rotating-cup instrument, a direction vane and a recording pressure trace. Match each to rainfall depth, humidity inference, wind speed, direction and pressure change respectively. The key should state any unfamiliar design. A fair interpretation does not require a learner to infer an invisible wick or an unreadable scale. Providing the relevant working part makes recognition an application of the physical principle, rather than a guess from where the picture is placed on the page.\n\n![Rain gauge, wet-and-dry bulb hygrometer and cup anemometer with their working parts](../../assets/images/ITEM-6137-1.6-008-INTERP-answer.png)",
