    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-1.6.03-18",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "These instruments connect observation to weather statistics, synoptic charts and climate records. An accurate sum or mean cannot compensate for an instrument measuring the wrong element or a record with an unknown interval. Check variable, unit, calibration, exposure and time before calculating. Then distinguish measured values from interpretations such as low pressure or an unusually wet period, which require a reference. This sequence creates a traceable account from apparatus to observation to conclusion, and it helps explain why apparently precise weather numbers can still carry important limitations.",
      "claim_ids": [
