      "block_id": "BL-6137-1.6.03-20",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "A combined thermometer image must also make the reset period explicit. Indices recorded at 09:00 can represent extremes since the previous reset, while a simultaneous dry-bulb value is the temperature then. The three values need not coincide. If the maximum index was not reset yesterday, today's indicated maximum may span a longer interval and cannot be compared uncritically with a neighbouring daily record. Marking the data limitation preserves information instead of inventing a correction.",
